OL,3,GNEWSA'An #8k service charge left me
OL,4,Aunable to pay bills'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA housing association has defended the
OL,7,Fcharges faced by its leaseholders after
OL,8,Fmany complained of huge bill increases
OL,9,Fto pay for maintenance.
OL,11,FCallum Maddern, who lives in Bath, said
OL,12,Fhe had seen his service charge increase
OL,13,Fsix-fold to more than #8,000 per year
OL,14,Fafter Curo said vital work needed doing
OL,15,Fon his accommodation block.
OL,17,F"I didn't have enough money to put the
OL,18,Fheating on," he said. "I had water on
OL,19,Fmy sink and coffee tables that was
OL,20,Ffreezing. I'd be lying in bed and I
OL,21,Fcould see my breath."
